      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: clarify plugin package live proof",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a documentation gap where plugin authors and maintainers could conflate source/archive installs, `npm-pack:` package proof, and trusted official plugin proof when validating plugin packages. That made it easy to miss runtime dependency mistakes or to overstate what a local tarball install proves for privileged plugin behavior.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds package/live-proof guidance in the OpenClaw testing skill and clarifies the plugin docs. The docs now separate managed package dependency proof via `npm-pack:` from catalog-linked official trust proof, and the plugin quickstart now calls out runtime dependency ownership plus the need for built JavaScript entries before package-install validation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPlugin authors and reviewers get a clearer path for validating release-candidate plugin packages. They can catch dependencies left in `devDependencies`, avoid manual repairs inside managed npm projects as final proof, and know when privileged official plugin behavior needs a second trusted install proof.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm docs:list`\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx`\n- `pnpm docs:check-links`\n- `pnpm format:docs:check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` clean after addressing review findings about `npm-pack:` trust scope, quickstart runtime dependencies, and peer install flags.\n",
        "branch": "feature/docs-plugin-package-live-proof",
